{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The rich shall not give more and the poor shall not give less.</b> The reason is that they shall bring the shekels at the stated equivalence. And it appears from this verse that if the poor man brought his shekel weighing less than half a shekel, he transgresses this negative commandment, for this verse is a prohibition. For if we were to say regarding \"the rich shall not give more\" that it is merely a negation, meaning that this suffices for him, we cannot interpret \"and the poor shall not give less\" in the same way. If so, both of them are prohibitions: if the rich man gave a single shekel more, or the poor man gave less, he transgressed a negative commandment. And perhaps what they would contribute from the collection boxes for what was lost and for future collections (Ketubot 108a) would correct this for them, for the poor man who gives less — the surplus of future collections is his, while from the rich man who gives more, the collectors do not take the excess, nor are funds merited to them through surpluses. And I have seen that the Ba'al Halakhot and all those who count the commandments did not mention this negative commandment."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "I resolved ראיתי לבעל הלכות as referring to the Ba'al Halakhot (i.e., the author of the Halakhot Gedolot). The phrase ולא יהו מזכין במותרות is rendered hyper-literally; the syntax is elliptical and the referent of the verbal construction is compressed in the original."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:18:47.844882919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}